<article class="env-lemma" id="031E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/031E">Lemma <span data-tag="031E">10.112.8</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a local homomorphism of local Noetherian rings. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R$ is regular, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S/\mathfrak m_ RS$ is regular, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R \to S$ is flat. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $S$ is regular. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00ON" data-tag="00ON">10.112.7</a> we have $\dim (S) = \dim (R) + \dim (S/\mathfrak m_ RS)$. Pick generators $x_1, \ldots , x_ d \in \mathfrak m_ R$ with $d = \dim (R)$, and pick $y_1, \ldots , y_ e \in \mathfrak m_ S$ which generate the maximal ideal of $S/\mathfrak m_ RS$ with $e = \dim (S/\mathfrak m_ RS)$. Then we see that $x_1, \ldots , x_ d, y_1, \ldots , y_ e$ are elements which generate the maximal ideal of $S$ and $e + d = \dim (S)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>